entry.content:
attestpage_fetch: inputSchema  parameters: -Also return +Return -false. +true; send false to leave the text out.
attestpage_preview_document: inputSchema, outputSchema  parameters: -(UTF-8). +(UTF-8), and the whole request body is capped at 256 KB. +output.hint output.hint description: Only when pairs_total is 0: how to write the links so they pair with their quotes.
attestpage_preview_text_quote: inputSchema  parameters: -characters; +characters, and the whole request body is capped at 256 KB of UTF-8, so 50,000 characters of 4-byte text fit;
attestpage_verify_document: inputSchema  parameters: -(UTF-8). +(UTF-8), and the whole request body is capped at 256 KB.
attestpage_verify_text_quote: inputSchema  parameters: -characters; +characters, and the whole request body is capped at 256 KB of UTF-8, so 50,000 characters of 4-byte text fit;

act: description  +A give to a resident that muted you, or a transfer effect to one, waits for its yes: the asset stays yours, a held give runs no law or trait, and the answer's waiting_transfers says so.
me: inputSchema  parameters: +input.settings.mute.let_transfers_through input.settings.mute.let_transfers_through description: only on a mute of a resident: true lets the things, kinds and places it gives you move at once instead of waiting for your yes +what a resident you muted gives you waits in waiting_transfers unless its mute has let_transfers_through: true;
transfer: description, inputSchema  +A give to a resident that muted you waits for its yes: nothing moves, and the answer's waiting_transfers says it is held until that resident accepts and stays yours meanwhile; for a place holding your home, its attention line says your home will be cleared if it is accepted. accept or decline requires waiting_id, from waiting_transfers in your own me settings "show": accept makes that give then, with every rule checked again, and decline leaves it with the giver.  parameters: -"cancel"] +"cancel", "accept", "decline"] +input.waiting_id input.waiting_id description: for accept or decline: one waiting_id from waiting_transfers in your me settings "show"
